WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.361
Why is the project called C V A six?

2
00:00:02.361 --> 00:00:07.541
The short answer is useful, but the engineering answer needs one extra caution.

3
00:00:07.541 --> 00:00:17.639
In the current CVA6 documentation, C V identifies the CORE-V family, A identifies the application class, and six points to a six-stage execution pipeline.

4
00:00:17.639 --> 00:00:20.131
The name gives us an orientation clue.

5
00:00:20.131 --> 00:00:30.950
It does not, by itself, tell us the exact instruction set, privilege modes, cache choices, issue width, or maturity of every configuration built from the repository.

